{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool","id":1086797,"title":"Demac's Exalted Character Creation Tool","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-02T14:33:35-07:00","id":1086797,"title":"Demac's Exalted Character Creation Tool","content":"So version 2.21 of my character creation tool is released. To those of you who are new to the tool, Demac's Exalted Character Creation Tool is specifically designed with the idea that you can go into the sheet and easily customize it to your game needs with just a little knowledge of Excel/Google Sheets.<br /> <br /> Version 2.21of my character creation tool is now available. I've made some major updates to it from version 2.2:<ul><li>First and foremost: IT SUPPORTS DRAGON-BLOODED CHARACTER CREATION (I'll pretend I hear some applause) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>You can now shift easily between creating a new exalt and an experienced Exalt at character creation.</li> <li>Caste and Aspect abilities now automatically update when the Caste/Aspect field is changed. That means with Solars, the list of available options for each ability (Caste, Favored, or Unfavored) automatically updates. For Dragon-Blooded, Aspect Abilities are automatically marked as such. Contrast this with version 2.2 and before where you had to update your template after changing your caste and you'll see that the workflow is much smoother.</li> <li>I corrected a mistake with the printable sheet that made it not update the Excellency/Specialty markers next to the ability name after character creation.</li> </ul>You should also notice that some charm names and all merits appear in a list in the appropriate field. The charm names are only those charm names that require an exact spelling for certain calculations to work correctly in the sheet (i.e. sorcery/necromancy charms, Ox-Body Technique, and all the Dragon-Blooded Excellency charms). If the charm you want isn't in this list, then you shouldn't worry because you wont' get an error message for populating the field with a value not in the list.<br /> <br /> As of today (4/17/18), we don't have the sorcery merits that will be offered in Dragon-Blooded: What Fire has Wrought so they obviously aren't on the merit list yet. I'll do a quick update of that list when we get them. Otherwise, enjoy version 2.21<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> DECCT is capable of handling these functions:<ul><li>Easy to use menus that automatically displays and hides sheets based on whether or not you are using them.</li> <li>Printable character sheets.</li> <li>Martial Arts attacks are calculated using the highest Martial Arts ability.</li> <li>Attacks made with a Martial Arts ability rated lower than your Highest Martial Arts ability.</li> <li>Attacks made with non-combat abilities.<ul><li>Example: The Burning Name</li> </ul></li> <li>Soak and Health Levels calculations that are effected by Charms and Merits.</li> <li>Charm calculations that automatically take into account free spells from sorcery charms.</li> <li>Weapon Tags that automatically effect the appropriate attack and damage pools.</li> <li>Automatic Bonus Point Calculation for New Characters.</li> <li>Automatic XP Calculation<ul><li>supports both regular and solar XP awards and calculations.</li> </ul></li> <li>Custom Character Creation Rules</li> <li>Custom Splat Creation (Found in the Engage the Exigence) menu option</li> <li>Siege Weapons (weapon calculation and the pools needed to use them)</li> <li>Customizing the Decisive attack pools that appear on the printable sheet.</li> </ul><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0Bx2jgxACzUj1MTlnbHZkcFdXaGc?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link to the Google Drive folder.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the link to the latest version.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":2346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","user":"Demac","date":". 04-17-2018, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T14:42:02-07:00","id":1086802,"title":"","content":"Probably should have mentioned that in order to reset the template properly, you should choose the Character type and Aspect/Caste before hitting the Reset button.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\